Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) - 1;
Q.media_capacity = (Number(Q.media_capacity) || 0) - 1;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left watches PiS fight its own auditor";
!}

The caucus decides that a fight between a governing party and its own appointee
is not our fight, and spends the week on the presidential campaign instead.

PiS and its auditor tear at each other without our assistance. Whatever the
audit chamber becomes over the next six years, it will remember that the Left
was not in the room when its independence was decided.

- @marshal_2019: Turn to the Marshal of the Sejm

@marshal_2019
# prose-audit: Grade B — Kuchciński's flights, his resignation and Witek's election are placed as one chain, and the misuse-of-office register is locked to the November audit-chamber decision; the pilots and crews who flew the routes remain a category.
title: The Marshal's aircraft
subtitle: The chair changed hands in August over government flights; the new chamber confirms it and the rules stay unwritten
face-image: img/poland/events/sejm-press-gallery.webp
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.marshal_2019_done = 1;
Q.pis_poll_momentum = (Number(Q.pis_poll_momentum) || 0) - 0.2;
Q.office_misuse_salience =
    (Number(Q.office_misuse_salience) || 0) + 20;
Q.institutional_issue_salience =
    (Number(Q.institutional_issue_salience) || 0) + 3;
Q.news_headline =
    "The new Sejm confirms the Marshal installed after her predecessor's flight scandal";
!}

= November 2019 — The office and the aircraft

The last Sejm's Marshal, <span class="party-pis"><b>Marek Kuchciński</b></span>, resigned in August after
journalists counted his flights on government aircraft: about a hundred of
them, a large number to his own constituency, several carrying his family.
There was no criminal charge. There was an itemised list, published, of a
public office being used as a car service, and a governing party that
discovered it could not defend the list for more than a fortnight.

<span class="party-pis"><b>Elżbieta Witek</b></span> took the chair the same day he left it and has held it
since. At the first sitting of the new chamber the majority simply confirms
her, which is a formality: PiS has the votes, the nomination and no reason to
reopen a question it closed in August.

So the chair is not in play and we should be honest with ourselves about that.
Forty-nine deputies out of four hundred and sixty cannot elect a Marshal and
will not. What is in play is everything the office does afterwards — the
calendar, the order paper, which divisions are re-run, and an expenses regime
that August proved is legible to anybody who can read a flight log.

This is the one sitting of the term at which the majority is embarrassed about
that office. It is the cheapest day in four years to put a rule on the record.

[? if nik_stance = "Institutional defence": Having spent this month defending
the audit chamber's independence, we have the one institution in the country
that can put flight logs, cars and residences into a statutory finding.?]
[? if nik_stance = "Resignation demanded": We spent this month demanding an
auditor's resignation over undeclared property, which makes a demand about a
Marshal's flights consistent and slightly repetitive.?]
[? if presidential_candidate != "Undecided": **[+ presidential_candidate +]** is
about to spend six months being asked what the Left would do differently with
public office, and this is the cheapest available answer.?]

- @marshal19_register
- @marshal19_rules
- @marshal19_candidate
- @marshal19_pass

@marshal19_register
title: Demand a published register of every official's use of state assets
subtitle: Requires an audit-chamber channel to be worth more than a press release; the register will eventually cover us too.
choose-if: nik_stance = "Institutional defence" or nik_stance = "Campaign centrepiece"
unavailable-subtitle: Without a working relationship with the audit chamber, a register demand from forty-nine deputies is a leaflet.
on-arrival: {!
Q.marshal_2019_response = "Asset register demanded";
Q.office_misuse_register = 1;
Q.office_misuse_salience =
    (Number(Q.office_misuse_salience) || 0) + 10;
Q.institutional_trust = (Number(Q.institutional_trust) || 0) + 6;
Q.nik_government_hostility =
    (Number(Q.nik_government_hostility) || 20) + 8;
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 4;
Q.administrative_reform_pressure =
    (Number(Q.administrative_reform_pressure) || 0) + 3;
Q.pis_relation = (Number(Q.pis_relation) || 0) - 4;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left asks for a public register of official flights, cars and residences";
!}

The demand is one page: flights, cars, official residences, published quarterly
with the office-holder's name against each. Not an accusation about Kuchciński
— a standing rule, applying to the Marshal, the ministers, the presidential
chancellery and every deputy including ours.

PiS cannot vote it down in the month it lost a Marshal to a flight log, so it
buries it in committee instead, which is a different and more useful kind of
defeat. The register text exists from now on and is taken down and dusted off
every time somebody senior is photographed getting off an aircraft.

- @poland_hub: Continue

@marshal19_rules
title: Table standing-order changes on re-run votes and disputed counts
subtitle: Aims at the Marshal's real power rather than her expenses; nobody will report it until the day it matters.
on-arrival: {!
Q.marshal_2019_response = "Standing orders";
Q.parliamentary_procedure_pressure =
    (Number(Q.parliamentary_procedure_pressure) || 0) + 12;
Q.constitutional_restraint =
    (Number(Q.constitutional_restraint) || 0) + 5;
Q.institutional_trust = (Number(Q.institutional_trust) || 0) + 4;
Q.parliament_visibility =
    (Number(Q.parliament_visibility) || 40) + 3;
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 1;
Q.media_capacity = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.media_capacity) || 0) - 1
);
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left proposes rules for re-run votes before anybody has re-run one";
!}

Our amendment says that a declared result may not be reversed without a
recorded recount, and that the reasons must be minuted. It is the dullest
document filed this month and it is aimed at the thing that will actually
matter: a Marshal who can decide that a division did not happen.

It goes nowhere. It is on the record, dated November 2019, and on the evening
in 2021 when a media-ownership vote is declared lost and then re-run, our
deputies are the only people in the chamber holding a text they wrote before
they needed it.

- @poland_hub: Continue

@marshal19_candidate
title: Nominate a counter-candidate to buy the speech
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. The vote is lost before it is called; the nomination speech is the only national platform on offer this month.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: There is no staff capacity to mount a nomination and its campaign.
