Q.resources = (Number(Q.resources) || 0) - 1;
Q.marshal_2019_response = "Symbolic candidacy";
Q.media_capacity = (Number(Q.media_capacity) || 0) + 4;
Q.left_poll_momentum =
    (Number(Q.left_poll_momentum) || 0) + 0.15;
Q.party_unity = (Number(Q.party_unity) || 0) + 3;
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 2;
Q.office_misuse_salience =
    (Number(Q.office_misuse_salience) || 0) + 6;
Q.pis_relation = (Number(Q.pis_relation) || 0) - 3;
Q.news_headline =
    "The returned Left puts up a candidate for the Marshal's chair";
!}

We do not pretend this is a contest. The nomination exists because a nominated
candidate gets the floor, and the floor is what we are buying: ten minutes,
broadcast live from the first sitting, on what the chair is for — the calendar,
the counts, the aircraft, and the difference between an office and a private
convenience.

Witek is confirmed by the margin everybody knew before the sitting began.

It is the first thing the new caucus does that most of the country actually
sees. Whether it was worth a resource depends entirely on whether we do
anything with the attention in December.

- @poland_hub: Continue

@marshal19_pass
title: Treat the Marshal's election as the majority's own business
subtitle: Costs nothing and concedes the chamber's rules to the people who will be writing them for four years.
on-arrival: {!
Q.marshal_2019_response = "No intervention";
Q.parliamentary_procedure_pressure =
    (Number(Q.parliamentary_procedure_pressure) || 0) + 2;
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) - 1;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Marshal is elected without an opposition proposal on the chamber's rules";
!}

Witek takes the chair. Our deputies vote against and say nothing further,
because a caucus of forty-nine has to choose what it spends November on and we
have chosen the presidential campaign.

Nobody remembers this in November. The chamber's rules are now entirely the
majority's, and the next four years will test how much that was worth saving a
week for.

- @poland_hub: Continue

@independence_2019
# prose-audit: Grade A — The returned caucus confronts the nationalist organisers through four distinct traditions, and every route now records who inherits the symbols, streets and political cost.
title: The Independence Day March
face-image: img/poland/events/independence-march-2021.webp
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.independence_march_2019_done = 1;
Q.last_independence_march_year = 2019;
